assertion  XSH.catan.014
anchor     functions/catan.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
says       (The page states this rule in terms of iz, which ranges over every
           value.) catan of the conjugate of z returns the conjugate of catan
           of z, part for part (equal values, zero signs included, NaN
           matching NaN), at ordinary points, at real-axis points where branch
           cuts lie, and at points with infinite parts and with a NaN real
           part.
note       The tag on this passage is the IEC 60559 Complex Floating-Point
           option; the test is NOTINUSE unless the C implementation claims it
           (Annex G of the C standard). No error is defined on this page, so
           errno is not examined; an exception is checked only when
           math_errhandling includes MATH_ERREXCEPT. Points with a NaN
           imaginary part are left out (and, for the odd and even rules,
           points with any NaN part): the sign of a NaN carries no required
           meaning. See Q-113.
test       t/014-conjugate-symmetry.c

assertion  XSH.catan.015
anchor     functions/catan.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
says       (The page states this rule in terms of iz, which ranges over every
           value.) catan of -z returns the negation of catan of z, part for
           part (equal values, zero signs included), at ordinary points, at
           real-axis points where branch cuts lie, and at points with infinite
           parts.
note       The tag on this passage is the IEC 60559 Complex Floating-Point
           option; the test is NOTINUSE unless the C implementation claims it
           (Annex G of the C standard). No error is defined on this page, so
           errno is not examined; an exception is checked only when
           math_errhandling includes MATH_ERREXCEPT. Points with a NaN
           imaginary part are left out (and, for the odd and even rules,
           points with any NaN part): the sign of a NaN carries no required
           meaning. See Q-113.
test       t/015-odd-symmetry.c
